AB  - Induction of labor (IOL) is an increasingly common obstetric procedure. Recent data demonstrates that over 40% of primiparous women, and over 30% of multiparous women, undergo labor induction. However, when IOL is attempted for a woman with an unfavourable cervix, other interventions used to assist the induction process, such as oxytocin or rupture of membranes, are connected with reduced effectiveness and high failure rates.
